1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:01,520
Your inventory feed

2
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:02,760
brings the dealership's

3
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,260
vehicles into AutoLander.

4
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,080
If your manager has already

5
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,380
connected the right feed,

6
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:08,480
keep that connection.

7
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,620
You only need

8
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:10,640
to check the vehicles.

9
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,200
To add your own source,

10
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,820
start in the left sidebar.

11
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:15,620
Click Configuration.

12
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,250
Across the top of that

13
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,580
page, choose Inventory Feeds.

14
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,490
Then click Add Feed.

15
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:23,030
You'll see two routes:

16
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:25,390
Website Scrape and Data Feed.

17
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,010
Let's start with a website.

18
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:28,840
For Cars dot com

19
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:30,650
or CarGurus, copy

20
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:32,120
the address of your dealership's

21
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,140
inventory page.

22
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:35,750
Back in AutoLander, choose Enter

23
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:37,990
a URL under Website Scrape.

24
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:39,160
Paste that address

25
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,480
into Website URL.

26
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,640
You can add

27
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,750
the dealer name as well.

28
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:43,980
Click Verify

29
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:45,270
and read the result.

30
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:46,950
When the source is ready,

31
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:48,810
choose Connect Website.

32
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:50,920
For a custom dealership website,

33
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:52,780
first ask AutoLander

34
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:54,220
to confirm that it's supported.

35
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:55,680
Now look at Data Feed.

36
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,640
This route uses inventory

37
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,180
supplied by your provider.

38
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:00,730
They can send a file,

39
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:01,980
provide a feed link,

40
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:03,980
or use the SFTP option.

41
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:05,200
On a dealer

42
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,220
or team plan,

43
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:07,650
AutoLander can help arrange

44
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,950
a connection with a provider

45
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:10,090
such as vAuto.

46
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:11,370
Have that connection

47
00:01:11,370 --> 00:01:12,440
set up with the correct

48
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:13,930
details before using it.

49
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,560
When the inventory loads,

50
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:17,420
click Post to Market

51
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,520
in the sidebar.

52
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:19,850
Check the location

53
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:21,330
and three familiar vehicles.

54
00:01:21,390 --> 00:01:22,410
Do their

55
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:23,520
prices and mileage match

56
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:24,900
your dealership's information?

57
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,990
Clear the search or filters

58
00:01:26,990 --> 00:01:28,750
if expected vehicles are hidden.

59
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,400
If the source is wrong,

60
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,760
dealer-account users

61
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:32,980
should tell their manager.

62
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,800
Individual users should

63
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,480
contact the AutoLander admin.

64
00:01:36,910 --> 00:01:38,510
In your workbook, note

65
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:39,680
your source and the three

66
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:40,700
vehicles you checked.
